    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras are positioned for a high-ceiling Saturday, anchored by **Yordan Alvarez** (81.16) and **Pete Crow-Armstrong** (80.98), who represent our clearest paths to production. **Yordan Alvarez** benefits from a favorable matchup against Brandon Young, carrying an elite xwOBA of 0.477 and a strong 16% SP skill advantage. Meanwhile, **Pete Crow-Armstrong** is our primary engine for the scarce stolen base category; his 100% success rate against the opposing pitcher\u2019s delivery cadence, combined with his lead-off spot against Zebby Matthews, makes him an indispensable start. We are also looking for significant contributions from **Colt Keith** (68.51) and **Junior Caminero** (68.24), both of whom capitalize on high-upside spots in the batting order and favorable platoon dynamics today.\n\nOur most difficult bench decision involved **Lars Nootbaar** (53.72), who narrowly missed the cut behind the outfield depth of **Christian Yelich** and **Nelson Velazquez**. While **Lars Nootbaar** offers a 19% SP skill advantage against Eduardo Rodriguez, the optimizer prioritized the higher base projection and dynamic platoon utility of **Nelson Velazquez**, who remains a threat with his 0.394 xwOBA. We are monitoring **Dillon Dingler**, **Trea Turner**, **Christian Yelich**, **Nelson Velazquez**, **Kyle Schwarber**, and **Carson Benge** closely, as their scores are currently based on projected lineups; any late-shift downward in their batting order could necessitate a pivot to our bench depth. We continue to hold **Hyeseong Kim**, **Josh Smith**, **Chase Meidroth**, **Jacob Gonzalez**, **Luis Pena**, and **Pedro Ramirez** in our development pipeline, as they remain in the minors and are unavailable for this slate.",
